  "slug": "coherent-unitary-6215",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend programmable unitary interferometers to optical neural networks, modular processors, and on-chip spectral measurement.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these preprints is the use of programmable interferometric networks as functional primitives in photonics. arXiv:2611.20390 proposes a logarithmic-depth butterfly interferometer architecture for parameter-efficient unitary transformations in coherent optical neural networks. arXiv:2611.21582 composes a modular processor from unitary tiles of fixed mixers and programmable phases, evaluated by numerical fitting. arXiv:2611.23667 uses unequal path lengths between two 8x8 unitary circuits on a universal silicon chip to achieve simultaneous spectral measurement and programmable filtering at 0.05 nm resolution. arXiv:2611.29115 instead realizes reconfigurable microwave photonic all-pass filters with a Kerr microcomb-driven transversal filter, so its link to the unitary-circuit theme is indirect. What is new is the joint emphasis on depth-efficient parameterization, modular tiling of unitary elements, and multifunctional use across computation, measurement, and filtering.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
